  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-86820512e180-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts: \"We'll now hear argument in Case 10-179, Stern v. Marshall.\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-86820512e180-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor: \"What's the authority at all for a bankruptcy court to adjudicate proof of claims, without violating Article III?\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-86820512e180-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia: \"A State can do that, but can the Federal Government make it the price that you pay for -- for going into a non-Article III tribunal?\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-86820512e180-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg: \"Will you include in that this 157(b)(5), because this whole thing would be a futile exercise if that tort claim comes -- comes out of the bankruptcy judge's -\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-86820512e180-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer: \"In which case?\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "86820512e1805b01b9a7a35b370b5a611b0ba10f75aa61f9e52feedf714d6289",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-86820512e180-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer: \"If -- if we were to decide this case, and suppose we decide every other question and suppose you lost, then wouldn't we send it back for you -- if you're right on that, for the Ninth Circuit to decide about that as an independent basis for no jurisdiction?\""
      }
    ],
